## E14 — advisory scan and inverse control

The Linux VM did not provide `cargo-audit`. The host's installed `cargo-audit`
0.22.1 was run against a newly cloned, temporary RustSec advisory database. The
tool was invoked as `cargo-audit audit`, which is the binary's direct equivalent
of the recorded `cargo audit` subcommand. The warning below is only an inability
to lock the sandbox's read-only shared crates.io cache; it did not prevent the
lockfile vulnerability scan.

$ /Users/stevemorin/.cargo/bin/cargo-audit audit --db /private/tmp/r67-rustsec-db --no-fetch
      Loaded 1243 security advisories (from /private/tmp/r67-rustsec-db)
warning: couldn't open crates.io index: I/O operation failed: failed to obtain lock file '/Users/stevemorin/.cargo/.package-cache'
    Scanning Cargo.lock for vulnerabilities (22 crate dependencies)
exit=0

$ sed -i '' 's/anyhow = "1.0.104"/anyhow = "=1.0.102"/' <temporary-control>/crates/rslb-cli/Cargo.toml
$ cargo generate-lockfile
    Updating crates.io index
     Locking 20 packages to latest Rust 1.96 compatible versions
      Adding anyhow v1.0.102 (available: v1.0.104)
exit=0

$ /Users/stevemorin/.cargo/bin/cargo-audit audit --db /private/tmp/r67-rustsec-db --no-fetch
      Loaded 1243 security advisories (from /private/tmp/r67-rustsec-db)
warning: couldn't open crates.io index: I/O operation failed: failed to obtain lock file '/Users/stevemorin/.cargo/.package-cache'
    Scanning Cargo.lock for vulnerabilities (22 crate dependencies)
Crate:     anyhow
Version:   1.0.102
