## E1–E12 cited-log support and direct citation spot checks

The cited evidence logs contain the command/result material claimed by their
corresponding empirical rows: E1 has 12 crate API blocks and 24 HTTP-200 markers;
E2 has 11 repository API records with star, archival, and push fields; E3 has
five issue-search calls and five numeric results; E4/E5 contain the package-page
and advisory-db controls plus `RUSTSEC-2026-0190`; E6/E7 contain the published
crate interfaces; E8/E9 contain the pinned Rust-source and authority anchors;
E10 contains R6.1, R7.6–R7.8, R8.2, and R9.6; E11 contains `EX_USAGE`,
`EX_CONFIG`, and `EX__MAX`; and E12 contains the reference manifests and
ripgrep's `ExitCode`/`BrokenPipe` branch.

Five direct `curl` spot checks independently confirmed the cited sources:

$ curl -w '%{http_code}' https://rustsec.org/packages/{anyhow,thiserror,signal-hook,ctrlc,inquire}.html
anyhow 200
thiserror 404
signal-hook 404
ctrlc 404
inquire 404

$ curl -w '%{http_code}' https://api.github.com/repos/RustSec/advisory-db/contents/crates/{anyhow,thiserror,signal-hook,ctrlc,inquire}
anyhow 200; thiserror 404; signal-hook 404; ctrlc 404; inquire 404
The `anyhow` page and directory listing name `RUSTSEC-2026-0190`. This confirms
that E4's zero-advisory conclusion rests on both paired controls, not a bare 404.

$ curl ctrlc-3.5.2.crate; grep 'pub fn set_handler' -A2 src/lib.rs
pub fn set_handler<F>(user_handler: F) -> Result<(), Error>
where
    F: FnMut() + 'static + Send,
The source says the `termination` feature sends SIGINT, SIGTERM, and SIGHUP to
that handler. This supports E6 only as an interface observation.

$ curl signal-hook-0.4.4.crate; grep 'pub fn register' -A5 src/flag.rs
pub fn register(signal: c_int, flag: Arc<AtomicBool>) -> Result<SigId, Error> {
    unsafe { low_level::register(signal, move || flag.store(true, Ordering::SeqCst)) }
}

$ curl inquire-0.9.4.crate; grep 'OperationCanceled\|OperationInterrupted' src/error.rs
OperationCanceled,
OperationInterrupted,
These are interface observations only. They do not demonstrate signal delivery,
prompt interruption, EPIPE handling, stream flushing, or destructor behavior.

$ curl rust-lang/rust/1.96.0/library/std/src/process.rs; grep process_exitcode, termination_trait_lib, and 'impl From<u8> for ExitCode'
`ExitCode`, `Termination`, and `From<u8> for ExitCode` are marked stable since 1.61.0.

